<title>HONG KONG: China involved in 90 pct of HK re-exports in 1996.</title>
<headline>China involved in 90 pct of HK re-exports in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>China was involved in HK$1.06 trillion, or 90 percent, of Hong Kong's total HK$1.19 trillion in re-exports in 1996, including flows to and from China, Census and Statistics department figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Re-exports accounted for 85 percent of the value of Hong Kong's total exports and 40 percent of its external trade in 1996, compared with 83 and 39 percent respectively a year earlier.</p>
<p>Most re-exports are for the processing of raw materials and semi-manufactured goods at Hong Kong-owned factories in China, with the finished goods coming back to Hong Kong.</p>
